# =============================================================================
# Job Flow — environment variables
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev. On hosts, set the SAME names in the dashboard.
#
# Hosts:
#   Local  → this file as `.env.local`
#   Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables (Production)
#   Render → Web Service → Environment (see “Render” section for build vs runtime)
#
# Do NOT mix Vercel Hobby clamp settings with Render no_clamp presets on the same
# deployment. Each host gets its own env set (see sections below).
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SHARED — required on every environment (local, Vercel, Render)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# InsForge
NEXT_PUBLIC_INSFORGE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_INSFORGE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional — default 90000 (90s). Raise if resume uploads time out on slow networks.
NEXT_PUBLIC_INSFORGE_TIMEOUT_MS=90000
# Optional — server API routes (requireAuth / jobs / agent). Defaults to 60000,
# or NEXT_PUBLIC_INSFORGE_TIMEOUT_MS if set.
# INSFORGE_SERVER_TIMEOUT_MS=60000

# Optional — per-attempt budget for profile load (default 45000). Retries on 504/timeout.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PROFILE_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS=45000

# PostHog (client)
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# PostHog (server-only) — dashboard charts (Feature 17). Without these,
# /api/dashboard/charts returns empty zero-filled series (HTTP 200).
# Create a personal API key in PostHog → Settings → Personal API keys (query scope).
POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY=
POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID=

# OpenRouter (server-only — never NEXT_PUBLIC_)
# Single key (still supported):
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-xxxxxxxx
# Multiple keys for rate-limit failover (preferred). Comma, semicolon, or newline separated:
OPENROUTER_API_KEYS=sk-or-v1-key1,sk-or-v1-key2,sk-or-v1-key3
AI_PROVIDER=openrouter
AI_MODEL=openrouter/free

# App environment:
#   development|dev  → no 429 on Resume AI pools (usage still tracked if Redis is set)
#   production|prod  → 429 when Redis (+ client IP for IP pool) are available
APP_ENV=development

# Redis — required in production for shared AI rate limits + usage bar
# (Extract + Generate + Find Jobs + Company Research).
# REDIS_URL=redis://default:password@host:6379
REDIS_URL=

# Shared Extract + Generate + Find Jobs + Company Research rate limits (server-only).
# Defaults: 3 / min, 15 / hour, 40 / day. Skipped when the user has BYOK OpenRouter keys.
# 429 only when APP_ENV=production|prod. Research: +1 per successful LLM call.
RESUME_AI_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=10
RESUME_AI_RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR=15
RESUME_AI_RATE_LIMIT_PER_DAY=40

# Per-IP abuse backstop (server-only). Always applies when REDIS_URL is set (incl. BYOK).
# 429 only in production. Defaults: 10 / min, 45 / hour, 120 / day.
RESUME_AI_IP_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=10
RESUME_AI_IP_RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR=45
RESUME_AI_IP_RATE_LIMIT_PER_DAY=120

# BYOK — AES-256-GCM for user OpenRouter keys on /profile (server-only).
# Required when users save personal keys. e.g. openssl rand -hex 32
BYOK_ENCRYPTION_SECRET=

# Adzuna (server-only). Required for Find Jobs discovery.
ADZUNA_APP_ID=
ADZUNA_APP_KEY=

# Browserbase (server-only). Required for Company Research (Feature 13).
BROWSERBASE_API_KEY=
BROWSERBASE_PROJECT_ID=

# Optional Pino log level (default info)
# LOG_LEVEL=info


# =============================================================================
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT — recommended extras for `.env.local`
# =============================================================================
# Long research budgets are fine on your machine (no Vercel 300s cap).
#
# APP_ENV=development
# RESEARCH_TIMEOUT_CLAMP=no_clamp
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RESEARCH_TIMEOUT_CLAMP=no_clamp
# BROWSERBASE_SESSION_TIMEOUT_SEC=780
# RESEARCH_OVERALL_TIMEOUT_MS=720000
# RESEARCH_GOTO_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# RESEARCH_EXTRACT_TIMEOUT_MS=180000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RESEARCH_CLIENT_TIMEOUT_MS=750000
#
# Keep EXTRACT so that: EXTRACT <= (OVERALL - GOTO - 90000) / 2


# =============================================================================
# VERCEL — set these in the Vercel dashboard (NOT Render)
# =============================================================================
# Vercel runs `next build` + serverless. It ignores Dockerfile / render.yaml.
# `output: "standalone"` in next.config does NOT break Vercel.
#
# --- Hobby (default) — KEEP CLAMPED ---
# Route keeps `export const maxDuration = 300` (Hobby hard max). App budgets must
# stay under ~300s or research will be killed mid-run.
#
# APP_ENV=production
# RESEARCH_TIMEOUT_CLAMP=clamp
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RESEARCH_TIMEOUT_CLAMP=clamp
# BROWSERBASE_SESSION_TIMEOUT_SEC=285
# RESEARCH_OVERALL_TIMEOUT_MS=270000
# RESEARCH_GOTO_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# RESEARCH_EXTRACT_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RESEARCH_CLIENT_TIMEOUT_MS=285000
# (Do NOT set RESEARCH_ROUTE_MAX_DURATION_SEC on Hobby — leave unset.)
#
# --- Pro only (optional) ---
# RESEARCH_TIMEOUT_CLAMP=no_clamp
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RESEARCH_TIMEOUT_CLAMP=no_clamp
# …plus raise `maxDuration` literal in app/api/agent/research/route.ts to 800,
# then use the longer ms values from the Render section.


# =============================================================================
# RENDER (Docker) — set these in the Render dashboard (NOT Vercel)
# =============================================================================
# Render builds the Dockerfile. Long-running Node — Vercel maxDuration is ignored.
# Blueprint defaults live in render.yaml; fill secrets with sync:false there or
# paste values in the dashboard.
#
# BUILD-TIME (must exist during `docker build` — baked into the client bundle):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_INSFORGE_URL
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_INSFORGE_ANON_KEY
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_RESEARCH_TIMEOUT_CLAMP
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_RESEARCH_CLIENT_TIMEOUT_MS
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_INSFORGE_TIMEOUT_MS          (optional)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_PROFILE_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS    (optional)
# On Render, dashboard env vars are available at build AND runtime for Docker.
#
# RUNTIME (secrets + server config — never commit):
#   APP_ENV=production
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEYS   (or OPENROUTER_API_KEY)
#   BYOK_ENCRYPTION_SECRET
#   REDIS_URL
#   ADZUNA_APP_ID / ADZUNA_APP_KEY
#   BROWSERBASE_API_KEY / BROWSERBASE_PROJECT_ID
#   POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY / POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID
#   AI_PROVIDER / AI_MODEL
#
# --- Research timeouts (no_clamp — recommended on Render) ---
# RESEARCH_TIMEOUT_CLAMP=no_clamp
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RESEARCH_TIMEOUT_CLAMP=no_clamp
# BROWSERBASE_SESSION_TIMEOUT_SEC=780
# RESEARCH_OVERALL_TIMEOUT_MS=720000
# RESEARCH_GOTO_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# RESEARCH_EXTRACT_TIMEOUT_MS=180000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RESEARCH_CLIENT_TIMEOUT_MS=750000
#
# After deploy: add https://YOUR-SERVICE.onrender.com/callback to InsForge
# allowedRedirectUrls. Prefer an always-on plan (free instances sleep).
#
# Full steps: README.md → “Deploy on Render (Docker)”.
